.nh
.TH "PB-TEAM-CANCEL-INVITE" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-team-cancel-invite - Cancel an outstanding invitation


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb team cancel-invite <team> <invitation> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Cancel an outstanding invitation

.PP
Cancel one outstanding invitation for the selected team at its expected generation. The invited account cannot accept that invitation afterward.

.PP
Teams use explicit membership and resource grants. Membership alone does not grant device use, ENV values, previews, or tunnels. Mutations use the current team generation to reject stale edits; read pb team get before retrying a conflicting change.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--generation\fP=0
	expected current team generation

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for cancel-invite

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print canonical JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-team(1)\fP
